@@ -0,0 +1,148 @@
+# Deploying the Tip Jar (static site on IPFS)
+
+The production site is a fully static Next.js export (`output: "export"`, `trailingSlash: true`, unoptimized images — see `packages/nextjs/next.config.ts`) that talks to **real Base (chain 8453)**. The switch from the local fork to Base is automatic when `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true` (`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts`). The burner wallet is disabled in that build.
+
+All commands run from the repo root unless a `cd` is shown.
+
+## 0. Prerequisites (once per contract release)
+
+### 0.1 TipJar must be deployed on Base
+
+The frontend reads the contract address from `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts`. Without a chain `8453` entry the site loads but can't find the contract.
+
+⚠️ This sends a real transaction on Base mainnet and costs real ETH gas. Tips go to `TIP_RECIPIENT`. Double-check the address.
+
+```bash
+# Put your own keys in packages/foundry/.env: ALCHEMY_API_KEY=..., ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=... (Etherscan V2 key, covers Base)
+yarn account:import              # or `yarn generate`; fund that address with a little ETH on Base
+TIP_RECIPIENT=0xYourTeamWallet yarn deploy --file DeployTipJar.s.sol --network base
+yarn verify --network base
+```
+
+Check it, then commit the updated `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts`:
+
+```bash
+TIPJAR_BASE=$(node -p "require('./packages/foundry/broadcast/DeployTipJar.s.sol/8453/run-latest.json').transactions.find(t => t.contractName === 'TipJar').contractAddress")
+echo $TIPJAR_BASE
+cast call $TIPJAR_BASE "usdc()(address)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org        # 0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913
+cast call $TIPJAR_BASE "recipient()(address)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org   # your TIP_RECIPIENT
+grep -n "8453" packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts                      # must show a chain 8453 block
+```
+
+### 0.2 Frontend keys
+
+Everything `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is baked into the static JS and is **public**. Use dedicated keys and restrict them to your domain.
+
+| Var | Why |
+| --- | --- |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` | Base RPC. Without your own key the app uses the shared SE-2 key after the public `mainnet.base.org` RPC, both rate-limited. In the Alchemy dashboard, allowlist your domain (e.g. `tipjar.yourname.eth.link`) and the gateway domain. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` | WalletConnect / mobile wallets. Allowlist the same domains at cloud.reown.com. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL` | Absolute base URL for OpenGraph/Twitter metadata. Without it `og:image` points to `localhost:3000`. |
+
+## 1. Build
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+
+export NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL="https://tipjar.yourname.eth.link"
+export NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY="<alchemy key>"
+export NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID="<walletconnect project id>"
+
+yarn ipfs:build
+```
+
+`yarn ipfs:build` runs exactly:
+
+```bash
+rm -rf .next out && NODE_OPTIONS='--require ./polyfill-localstorage.cjs' NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true yarn build
+```
+
+- `rm -rf .next out` — never ship stale output.
+- `polyfill-localstorage.cjs` — Node 25+ has a broken global `localStorage` that crashes prerendering; `--require` also patches Next's build workers. Harmless on older Node.
+- `yarn build` = lint + `next build` with type checking (do **not** set `NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR`).
+- `Warning: --localstorage-file was provided without a valid path` lines on Node 25 are noise.
+
+## 2. Verify the build before uploading
+
+Still in `packages/nextjs`:
+
+```bash
+# Every route is a directory with index.html (needed for IPFS gateways)
+ls out/index.html out/debug/index.html out/404.html
+
+# Metadata points to production, not localhost
+grep -o '<title>[^<]*' out/index.html                          # USDC Tip Jar
+grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>' out/index.html       # https://tipjar.yourname.eth.link/thumbnail.jpg
+grep -c "localhost:3000" out/index.html                        # 0
+
+# The Base TipJar address is in the bundle (TIPJAR_BASE from step 0.1)
+grep -rli "$TIPJAR_BASE" out/_next/static/chunks | head -1     # must print a file
+
+# Not stale: no source file newer than the build output (must print nothing)
+find app components contracts hooks services utils scaffold.config.ts next.config.ts -newer out -type f
+
+# Local preview of the exact static output
+python3 -m http.server 4000 -d out
+#   → open http://localhost:4000 : "USDC Tip Jar", wallet connect asks for Base, tip feed loads,
+#     "Tips go to" shows your TIP_RECIPIENT. Ctrl+C when done.
+```
+
+## 3. Upload to IPFS (BuidlGuidl IPFS)
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+yarn bgipfs upload config init -u https://upload.bgipfs.com -k <BGIPFS_API_KEY>   # once per machine
+yarn bgipfs upload out                                                             # prints the CID
+export CID=<printed CID>
+```
+
+A real code change always yields a new CID. Same CID as last release = you uploaded the old build.
+
+(`yarn ipfs` does build + config + upload in one go, but the step-by-step path above lets you verify before uploading.)
+
+## 4. Post-deploy verification
+
+The build uses root-absolute asset paths (`/_next/...`), so it must be served from a domain root: an ENS gateway (`.eth.link`) or a subdomain gateway. `community.bgipfs.com/ipfs/<CID>` redirects to `<CID>.ipfs.community.bgipfs.com`, so always pass `-L`.
+
+```bash
+GW="https://community.bgipfs.com/ipfs/$CID"
+
+# Routes return 200 (after redirect)
+for p in "" "debug/" "debug"; do
+  echo "/$p -> $(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -L "$GW/$p")"
+done
+
+# Page + metadata
+curl -s -L "$GW/" | grep -o '<title>[^<]*'
+curl -s -L "$GW/" | grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>'
+
+# JS assets load from the domain root
+SITE=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{url_effective}' -L "$GW/")        # https://<CID>.ipfs.community.bgipfs.com/
+CHUNK=$(curl -s "$SITE" | grep -o '/_next/static/chunks/[^"]*\.js' | head -1)
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "$CHUNK -> %{http_code}\n" "${SITE%/}$CHUNK"   # 200
+
+# Production contract answers on Base
+cast call $TIPJAR_BASE "totalTipped()(uint256)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org
+```
+
+Then in a browser at `https://<CID>.ipfs.community.bgipfs.com/`:
+
+1. Title is "USDC Tip Jar"; no burner wallet in the connect modal.
+2. Connect a wallet on another chain → the app offers "Switch to Base".
+3. Feed loads (or "No tips yet"), "Tips go to" shows the right recipient.
+4. Send a tiny real tip (e.g. 0.01 USDC): Approve → Tip → tip appears in the feed, "Total tipped" increases.
+5. Reject a transaction in the wallet → the UI recovers (buttons re-enabled).
+
+## 5. Optional: ENS name
+
+Set the content hash of e.g. `tipjar.yourname.eth` to `ipfs://<CID>` in the ENS app (Records → Content Hash), then:
+
+```bash
+NAME=tipjar.yourname.eth
+RESOLVER=$(cast call 0x00000000000C2e074eC69A0dFb2997BA6C7d2e1e "resolver(bytes32)(address)" $(cast namehash $NAME) --rpc-url https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com)
+cast call $RESOLVER "contenthash(bytes32)(bytes)" $(cast namehash $NAME) --rpc-url https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com   # non-empty, matches CID
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -L "https://$NAME.link/"                                                         # 200 (gateway cache: 5-15 min)
+curl -s -L "https://$NAME.link/" | grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>'
+```
+
+`NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL` must match this final URL; if you change the domain, rebuild and re-upload.
